@@ -3,6 +3,14 @@
 Every correction is REINFORCE with a detached weight w(r) on the ratio
 r = p/q of trainer (p) to sampler (q) probabilities, per token or per
 sequence.
+
+Sampler-centred score (default, with or without a correction): each token's
+score grad log p(x) is replaced by grad [log p(x) - E_q log p(Y)], where the
+expectation over the sampler's next-token distribution q is taken on the
+top-k logprobs the sampler returns. The subtracted term has zero mean under
+q for every position, so a mismatched sampler no longer pushes the trainer's
+logits toward q (see REPORT.md). It is identical to the usual score in
+expectation when q = p.
 """
 import math
 from typing import NamedTuple
